$ diva run abs.ml
7
[exit 0]

$ diva check abs.ml
no runtime error is possible
[exit 0]

$ diva opt abs.ml
(let abs = (fun x -> (if (x < 0) then (0 - x) else x)) in (let dist = (fun a -> (abs (a - 10))) in (dist 3)))
[exit 0]

$ diva hints abs.ml
x#0 : -7
a#1 : 3
[exit 0]

$ diva cert --check abs.ml
[diva] running Lean on abs.lean
wrote abs.lean
certificate checked by Lean: the program never fails
[exit 0]

$ diva prove --check -o prove.lean abs.ml
[diva] running Lean on prove.lean
wrote prove.lean
checked by Lean: the functions meet their contracts, and the top-level expressions don't fail
[exit 0]

